-- Kept on ASSUME deliberately (IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.1, R0: ASSUME is deprecated): the relational middle end lowers a top-level ASSUME to an input predicate, and this file is that widening's exhibit. NOT publishable as a web API since R-X4 (§11.21) — see header.
-- The ASSUME seed: the second source of an `RInput` predicate.
--
-- A top-level ASSUME is a name the module states a signature for and never
-- defines — which is exactly what an input predicate is, so it lowers to one
-- (`L4.Relational.IR`, RInput). This file is the golden for that widening, and
-- carries one instance of every shape it has to get right:
--
--   * `ASSUME T IS A TYPE` becomes an ABSTRACT CATEGORY, printed in its own
--     block. It is category-shaped like a DECLAREd record (same `RSRecord`
--     sort, so no consumer gains a case) and has no fields, so it is not in
--     `records:` — a reader of a golden has to be able to tell "declared, no
--     field projected" from "assumed, has none".
--
--   * A BOOLEAN-valued ASSUME lowers with `rpResult = Nothing`: the output
--     argument is dropped, exactly as for a boolean DECIDE, which is what lets
--     `NOT` over it become a signed goal rather than an equation. Read the
--     golden: `is authorised` is `input …/1 : (goal)` and appears in a clause
--     as a bare `is authorised(Person_0)`.
--
--   * A VALUE-valued ASSUME keeps its output argument: `conduct/1 : Behaviour`.
--
--   * `NOT` over an ASSUMEd boolean is an `RNotCall`, and signs its dependency
--     edge NEGATIVE — which is what lifts `may issue a notice` into stratum 1.
--     The Blawx leg turns that into classical `-p` (R5) precisely BECAUSE the
--     callee's kind is `RInput`: an input that was never stated must fail
--     loudly rather than read as false.
--
--   * `@desc` and `@ref` on an ASSUME are carried to the predicate, separately
--     (`desc:` / `ref:` in the golden). Without them an ASSUME-style module
--     would hand an ontology-bearing target a declaration with no prose and no
--     citation — and this corpus shape has nothing else to offer, since there
--     are no field declarations to annotate.
--
--   * REACHABILITY. `affects the quality of life` is ASSUMEd and never called;
--     `Locality` is ASSUMEd as a type and sorts nothing. Neither appears in the
--     golden. That gate is what makes the widening additive — a module with no
--     ASSUMEs cannot gain a predicate — and it mirrors what a DECLAREd field
--     that no projection reads already does.
--
-- The two exported decisions differ in their annotations on purpose: the first
-- carries prose and a citation, the second a citation only. The Blawx leg's
-- section text falls back `@desc` -> `@ref` -> stub, so the pair pins two of
-- those three arms in one file.
--
-- == This file lowers here and cannot be published as a web API
--
-- Both spellings — the one below and `ASSUME f IS A FUNCTION FROM Person TO
-- BOOLEAN` — lower identically (the arrow spine is flattened), and since R-X4
-- (2026-09-07, built 2026-09-08) an `@export` that reads EITHER is refused:
-- a request carries values, and an assumed predicate is a rule. So `l4 check`
-- on this file reports six refusals and nothing is wrong with it. The lowering
-- is unaffected on purpose — `L4.Cli.Blawx.loadBlawxDoc` and this suite's own
-- harness step over exactly those two diagnostics by name, via
-- `L4.TypeCheck.Types.isExportPublicationRefusal`, because an assumed predicate
-- is an ordinary logic-program input. See IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.21; the
-- app-form spelling stays because it is the exhibit, not because it exports.
--
-- There are no #EVAL / #ASSERT directives, and that is not an oversight: ASSUME
-- is uninterpreted, so `l4 run` cannot anchor an expectation here at all. A
-- differential harness for a module in this style takes its oracle from a
-- semantically equivalent GIVEN-record spelling of the same logic, not from
-- this file.

§ `Community protection notices`

ASSUME Person IS A TYPE
ASSUME Behaviour IS A TYPE

-- Sorts nothing: no admitted signature mentions it, so it earns no `abstract
-- categories:` entry.
ASSUME Locality IS A TYPE

@desc an authorised person within the meaning of section 53
@ref s 43(1) Anti-social Behaviour, Crime and Policing Act 2014
GIVEN p IS A Person
ASSUME `is authorised` p IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 53(1)(a)
GIVEN p IS A Person
ASSUME `has surrendered authority` p IS A BOOLEAN

@desc the conduct the person is engaged in
GIVEN p IS A Person
ASSUME conduct p IS A Behaviour

GIVEN b IS A Behaviour
ASSUME `is unreasonable` b IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN b IS A Behaviour
ASSUME `is of a persistent nature` b IS A BOOLEAN

-- Called by nothing: absent from `predicates:`.
GIVEN b IS A Behaviour
ASSUME `affects the quality of life` b IS A BOOLEAN

@export whether the person may issue a community protection notice
@ref s 43(1)
GIVEN person IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may issue a notice` IF
       `is authorised` person
  AND      NOT `has surrendered authority` person
  AND  `is unreasonable` (conduct person)

@export
@ref s 43(1)(a)
GIVEN person IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a persistent nuisance` IF
  `is of a persistent nature` (conduct person)
